From 5ced27f8a6d64e0b8135302f67ec583dd083c8b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 18:04:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 55/56] video: rockchip: mpp: bounds-check register-translation
 imports

Two out-of-bounds writes into struct mpp_task's fixed 80-entry
translation storage are reachable from an unprivileged MPP job with
crafted register-translation requests. Both corrupt adjacent task fields
(state, abort_request, delayed_work) during task assembly, before any
hardware runs.

- mpp_task_attach_fd() rejected only mem_count > MPP_MAX_REG_TRANS_NUM,
  then wrote &task->mem_regions[mem_count]. At mem_count == 80 the test
  is false and element 80 is already one past the 80-element array.
  Reachable by repeating one valid dma-buf fd across 81 attachment
  slots. Fail closed with >=.
- mpp_extract_reg_offset_info() floored the element count
  (cnt = size / 8) for its bound check but then copied the raw
  req->size bytes, so a non-multiple size (e.g. 647 -> cnt 80) copied up
  to seven bytes past the 80-element elem[] array. Reject sizes that are
  not a whole number of elements and copy only the validated length.

These are the AV1-R1 and AV1-R8 findings from the forward-port lifetime
audit; the AV1 backend's larger 103-translation demand still needs the
attachment storage resized, but that is a separate change -- rejecting
the overflow is the immediate memory-safety fix and does not affect
normal decode, which stays well under 80 attachments. The BSP donor has
the same '>' guard and unchecked copy length.

Signed-off-by: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
index b981bcbb1ae94..0fe7fe01467f5 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
@@ -1988,7 +1988,7 @@ mpp_task_attach_fd(struct mpp_task *task, int fd)
 	if (fd <= 0 || !dma || !mpp)
 		return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
 
-	if (task->mem_count > mem_num) {
+	if (task->mem_count >= mem_num) {
 		mpp_err("mem_count %d must less than %d\n", task->mem_count, mem_num);
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 	}
@@ -2123,14 +2123,25 @@ int mpp_extract_reg_offset_info(struct reg_offset_info *off_inf,
 {
 	int max_size = ARRAY_SIZE(off_inf->elem);
 	int cnt = req->size / sizeof(off_inf->elem[0]);
+	u32 size = cnt * sizeof(off_inf->elem[0]);
 
+	/*
+	 * Reject a byte count that is not a whole number of elements: the
+	 * check below floors to complete elements, but the copy used the raw
+	 * req->size, so a non-multiple size (e.g. 647 -> cnt 80) copied up to
+	 * seven bytes past the 80-element array into adjacent task fields.
+	 */
+	if (req->size != size) {
+		mpp_err("invalid reg offset size %u\n", req->size);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 	if ((cnt + off_inf->cnt) > max_size) {
 		mpp_err("count %d, total %d, max_size %d\n",
 			cnt, off_inf->cnt, max_size);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 	if (copy_from_user(&off_inf->elem[off_inf->cnt],
-			   req->data, req->size)) {
+			   req->data, size)) {
 		mpp_err("copy_from_user failed\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
